<title>USA: Nasdaq corrects software problem.</title>
<headline>Nasdaq corrects software problem.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Nasdaq spokeswoman said a software problem occurring shortly after the 1600 EDT/2000 GMT market close on Thursday has been corrected, adding that all quotes on indices and stocks are now official.</p>
<p>The Nasdaq composite fell 1.15 points, officially closing at 1372.60, and a total of 551,355,500 shares changed hands, according the spokeswoman.</p>
<p>Advancing issues led decliners 2018 to 1883.</p>
</text>
